# Trivy findings that are not actionable here, each with the reason it is not.
# This file is for advisories with no fix and no reachable path — never for a
# real vulnerability someone would rather not deal with today. Anything listed
# here must also be clean under govulncheck, which reads reachability.

# GO-2026-5932 — golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp is unmaintained and unsafe by
# design. The advisory is filed against the whole golang.org/x/crypto module
# and has NO fixed version, so no upgrade clears it.
#
# Trellis does not import openpgp. `go list -deps ./...` shows the x/crypto
# packages actually in the build are argon2 and blake2b (the password hash) and
# chacha20poly1305/cryptobyte pulled in by the TLS stack — zero openpgp.
# govulncheck agrees: "0 vulnerabilities ... 1 vulnerability in modules you
# require, but your code doesn't appear to call [it]".
#
# Dropping the dependency is not an option that exists: argon2 lives in this
# module, and it is what seed and stem hash with too.
#
# Re-check when x/crypto finally removes openpgp, at which point this line
# should be deleted rather than renewed.
GO-2026-5932
